        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Sealing an epoxy garage floor</strong> is about UV stability and sacrificial wear, not waterproofing. On a new floor, coat inside the recoat window and skip the sanding entirely. On an older one, degrease, abrade to a uniform dull, vacuum obsessively, and put down two thin coats of a two-part aliphatic urethane or a polyaspartic.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Recoat when the wheel paths lose gloss and the rest of the floor has not — that is <strong class="text-white">a weekend and a few hundred dollars</strong>. Wait until the color layer wears through and the same floor becomes a grind-and-reinstall job costing ten times as much.
          </p>
        </div>
